WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.304
In the last years of the Southern Song, Wen Tianxiang spent all his family fortune raising troops to resist the Yuan, vowing to defend his country to the death and never retreat.

00:00:08.654 --> 00:00:17.966
After his defeat and capture, the Yuan army threatened and tempted him to surrender, but he straightened his back and refused to kneel.

00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:25.540
In prison, by the faint lamplight, he wrote the immortal poem 'Crossing the Lonely Sea'.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:30.282
His brush never stopped, every stroke full of deep feeling.

00:00:30.632 --> 00:00:38.336
'Who since ancient times has not died? Leave a loyal heart to shine in history.' These words have been passed down through the ages.

00:00:38.686 --> 00:00:46.390
Sunlight shone into the dark cell, as if lighting up his loyal, unyielding heart.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:54.492
Later generations built a shrine for him, where the candle flames burn forever, eternally remembering this great and loyal minister.

00:00:54.842 --> 00:00:57.914
Every year, many people come to lay flowers in tribute.

